{
  "assessment": "This diff adds three new write entry points (importer, scheduler, webhook) that each iterate over operations and call `project.write()` directly. None of the paths consult project state or archive flags before mutating, meaning they can still record revisions against archived projects like Borealis. This breaks the explicit contract in `docs/archiving.md` that an archived project must not change again.\n\nDefects:\n1. Unconditional mutation in `workspace/importer.py`\n   - call: Invoking `apply(index, ops)` where an operation targets an archived project (e.g., Borealis)\n   - expected: Archive validation detects the read-only state and rejects or skips the write operation\n   - actual: `project.write()` executes immediately with no guard, mutating archived history\n\n2. Unconditional mutation in `workspace/scheduler.py`\n   - call: Invoking `apply(index, ops)` via the scheduler path targeting an archived project\n   - expected: Scheduler path respects archive contract and prevents state updates on read-only projects\n   - actual: Direct field write proceeds without checking status, violating the no-change guarantee\n\n3. Unconditional mutation in `workspace/webhook.py`\n   - call: Invoking `apply(index, ops)` via webhook handler targeting an archived project\n   - expected: Inbound data is filtered or rejected if target project is archived\n   - actual: Payload triggers unconditional `project.write()`, allowing post-archive revisions",
  "findings": [
    {
      "actual": "`project.write()` executes immediately with no guard, mutating archived history",
      "at": "workspace/importer.py",
      "call": "Invoking `apply(index, ops)` where an operation targets an archived project (e.g., Borealis)",
      "defect": "Unconditional mutation in workspace/importer.py",
      "expected": "Archive validation detects the read-only state and rejects or skips the write operation"
    },
    {
      "actual": "Direct field write proceeds without checking status, violating the no-change guarantee",
      "at": "workspace/scheduler.py",
      "call": "Invoking `apply(index, ops)` via the scheduler path targeting an archived project",
      "defect": "Unconditional mutation in workspace/scheduler.py",
      "expected": "Scheduler path respects archive contract and prevents state updates on read-only projects"
    },
    {
      "actual": "Payload triggers unconditional `project.write()`, allowing post-archive revisions",
      "at": "workspace/webhook.py",
      "call": "Invoking `apply(index, ops)` via webhook handler targeting an archived project",
      "defect": "Unconditional mutation in workspace/webhook.py",
      "expected": "Inbound data is filtered or rejected if target project is archived"
    }
  ]
}
